We have submitted the recolored image of Baker Berry Library. All of the regions are a uniform reddish color because our code amplifies the hues
of the original image in the recolored image. Some of the small areas of baker berry are not recolored, similar to the professors. We decided to
keep the original 50 pixel minimum for regions to be added to the arrayList of arrayLists. This makes sure that regions that are too small aren't
added. We check the color of each pixel by taking the absolute value of red, blue, and green values individually. Only if all of them are within
the 20 benchmark, are they added to the current Region arrayList.

Our CamPaint code allows the user to set a target color using a mouse press can do one of 3 things:
When the user presses the ‘w’ key, the program will display the unaltered video
When the user presses the ‘r’ key, the program will highlight the color of all of the regions in the screen of 50+ pixels that roughly have the
same color as the target color
When the user presses the ‘p’ key, the program displays a blank white screen and begins “painting” the screen with the largest region of the target
 color on the screen with a blue color.

In terms of limitations, the lighting of the room you’re in while using this program has a major impact on its effectiveness, because shadows can
have a major effect on colors, making the program unable to detect the uniform colors.



